NAME: Evening brief
OWNER: TMEC Command
ACCOUNT: business
WHEN: Every weekday at 5:47 PM (Australia/Brisbane)
MILESTONE: M3
STATUS: Created paused. Turned on only after Tommy says yes.
---
Switch check: read /workspace/tmec-team/context/routines-on.md. If "Evening brief" isn't listed there as "on" or "test", append "<time> · Evening brief · SKIPPED_OFF" to /workspace/tmec-team/log/runs-<YYYY-MM>.md and stop.
Test mode: if it's listed as "test", send every message to the owner only (Tommy, or Justin's team in a test run), never to a channel or anyone else, and start each message with "TEST". Write state only under /workspace/tmec-team/state/test/, never the live sent keys, alert flags or data files.
Stop check: if /workspace/tmec-team/state/EXTERNAL_WRITES_STOPPED exists, append "<time> · Evening brief · SKIPPED_STOPPED" to the run log and stop, sending nothing. The one exception: pause or unschedule your own already-scheduled sends, as your skill's stop section says. Whoever stopped the team already told Tommy.
Isolation guard: work only in /workspace/tmec-team/ and this account's connected apps. If /workspace/tmec-team/context/owner.md is missing, append "<time> · Evening brief · NO_CLIENT_SOURCE" to the run log and stop. Read other bots' files only where your skill says so; never write them, and never use another bot's logins or memory.
Lean run: read only what this job needs. Stop with NO_CHANGE only where the job below says nothing changed: append "<time> · Evening brief · NO_CHANGE" to the run log and stop. A report that always goes out never stops here.
Run log: when you finish, append "<time> · Evening brief · EXECUTED · <one-line result>" to /workspace/tmec-team/log/runs-<YYYY-MM>.md, or FAILED with the reason. A source you couldn't read is UNKNOWN in your output, never zero.

Use the evening-brief skill. Read today's notes from every bot in /workspace/tmec-team/daily/<today>/, today's decisions in /workspace/tmec-team/approved/decisions/, the items still in /workspace/tmec-team/approved/pending/, and today's run-log lines. If no bot did anything today, nothing was decided and nothing is waiting, write NO_CHANGE and stop. Otherwise send Tommy under 120 words: what got done today (one line per bot that did something, with its number), what he decided, and what's waiting on him tomorrow (numbered). Save it to /workspace/tmec-team/daily/<today>/evening.md and add it under the morning brief in /workspace/tmec-team/vault/Daily/<today>.md.
